.TH FMT_ESCAPECHARQUOTEDPRINTABLE 3 "15 Mar 2023" "CB" "Library Functions"

.SH NAME
fmt_escapecharquotedprintable \- Escape characters for quoted printable format

.SH SYNOPSIS
.IB #include <lib/fmt.h>

.IB size_t
.IB fmt_escapecharquotedprintable(char* dest, int c);

.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBfmt_escapecharquotedprintable\fR function escapes characters for quoted printable format. It takes a destination buffer and a character as arguments. The function escapes the character if it is not in the printable ASCII range, otherwise it copies the character unchanged.

The function takes the following parameters:
.IB char*
A pointer to the destination buffer.
.IB int
The character to escape.

The function returns the number of bytes written to the destination buffer.

The \fBfmt_escapecharquotedprintable\fR function is intended to be used to escape characters for quoted printable format, such as non-ASCII characters and control characters.

.SH EXAMPLES
The following example demonstrates how to use the \fBfmt_escapecharquotedprintable\fR function to escape characters for quoted printable format:

.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <lib/fmt.h>

int main() {
    char dest[10];
    int c = 0x80;

    size_t written = fmt_escapecharquotedprintable(dest, c);

    printf("Written %d bytes: %s\n", written, dest);

    return 0;
}
.nef